{"action":"","actor":"","alternative_quotes":["(a) Within three consecutive calendar days, comply with the applicable central accumulation area requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code; or","(b) Remove the excess from the satellite accumulation area within three consecutive calendar days to either:

(i) A central accumulation area operated in accordance with the applicable requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code;

(ii) An on-site permit by rule or permitted treatment, storage, or disposal facility; or

(iii) An off-site designated facility."],"choice_text":"Within three consecutive calendar days, the generator must either comply with applicable central accumulation area requirements, or remove the excess to one of three designated destinations: a compliant central accumulation area, an on-site permitted/permit-by-rule facility, or an off-site designated facility.","claimants":[],"concepts":[],"effective_periods":[],"jurisdiction":"","kind":"requirement","logic_text":"","modality":"must","object":"","scope_text":"A generator who accumulates either acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or non-acute hazardous waste in excess of the amounts listed in paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-15 at or near any point of generation","summary":"A generator who accumulates either acute hazardous waste listed in rule 3745-51-31 or paragraph (E) of rule 3745-51-33 of the Administrative Code or non-acute hazardous waste in excess of the amounts listed in paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-15 at or near any point of generation shall, within three consecutive calendar days, comply with the applicable central accumulation area requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code, or remove the excess from the satellite accumulation area within three consecutive calendar days to either: (i) a central accumulation area operated in accordance with the applicable requirements in paragraph (B) of rule 3745-52-16 or paragraph (A) of rule 3745-52-17 of the Administrative Code; (ii) an on-site permit by rule or permitted treatment, storage, or disposal facility; or (iii) an off-site designated facility.","typed_values":[]}
